<HelloFraandsPage updated="2026-10-28" title="Women's safety" summary="Apni baat, apni marzi — aap tay karein kaun aapko call kar sakta hai." review={true} related={[{href:'/safety',label:'Safety centre'},{href:'/community-guidelines',label:'Community guidelines'},{href:'/lgbtq',label:'LGBTQ+ safety'}]}>
<p>Women influencers decide who can call them. Your number is always masked, you can decline any call, and the <strong>#</strong> key ends a call and blocks the caller.</p>
<h2 id="women-only-channels">Women-only channels</h2>
<p>A <strong>Women-only channel</strong> (the category is called <strong>Women-to-Women</strong>) is a channel started by an Aadhaar-verified woman, for Aadhaar-verified women. Both the influencer and the caller must be Aadhaar-verified women. It shows a pink <strong>Women only</strong> tag on the profile and in Reels, and it is visible to everyone in Explore, search and Google. Only Aadhaar-verified women can call, book, join the queue or ask to be notified.</p>
<h2>Who can start one</h2>
<p>You do not need a YouTube or Instagram account. In our app you pick Women-to-Women as a category and verify your Aadhaar with an OTP (DigiLocker if the OTP does not work). Your Aadhaar must show female. Then you record your 10 to 20 second live intro video. There is no separate selfie video. A person from our team approves you, and your channel goes live. A Women-only channel always needs Aadhaar, and you can also add Social media verification if you have a YouTube, Instagram or Facebook account.</p>
<h2>Who can call</h2>
<p>To call a Women-only channel you verify your Aadhaar once (it must show female). No selfie video is needed. If you are not verified and you tap Call, Book or Join queue, you see: &ldquo;This is a women-only channel. Only Aadhaar-verified women can talk to her.&rdquo; with <strong>Verify now</strong> and <strong>Not now</strong>. If you are verified but your Aadhaar does not show female, you see: &ldquo;Sorry, this channel is for women only.&rdquo; Our system also checks this. You verify once, and it works for every Women-only channel.</p>
<p>Verified people show a green <strong>verified</strong> badge. Verification confirms who someone is. It does not guarantee how anyone will behave, so every safety rule below still applies.</p>
<p>Your Aadhaar number and your video are seen only by you and our verification team. We keep only the last 4 digits of the Aadhaar number. Everyone must be 18 or older. Never share your number, address or identity documents on a call.</p>
<h2>What you can talk about</h2>
<p>Everyday life, work, family, relationships and personal experiences are welcome. You may discuss experiences such as periods, PCOS, pregnancy or menopause without being treated as making sexual conversation. Harassment, sexual pressure and abuse remain reportable. Influencers offer conversation, not diagnosis, treatment, therapy or counselling.</p>
<h2>Your boundaries come first</h2>
<ul><li>You can decline a call, stop a conversation or leave without explaining why. Payment never buys permission to cross a boundary.</li><li>Keep your number, address, workplace, social accounts and payment details private. Never share an OTP, identity document or another person's story.</li><li>Do not move a conversation to private contact, arrange meetings, send money or accept pressure to do so.</li><li>Number masking hides each participant's phone number from the other. It cannot hide details you say aloud or prevent someone recognising your voice.</li></ul>
<aside class="hf-before-call" aria-labelledby="hf-before-call-title">
  <h2 id="hf-before-call-title">Before you call</h2>
  <p>You can talk about periods, PCOS, pregnancy, menopause, family stress, or anything else on your mind. You never have to share documents, intimate photos, contact details, or stay on a call that feels wrong. Hang up if you want to. A report asks the team to review what happened; it is not an emergency alert.</p>
</aside>
<h2>Influencer controls</h2>
<p>The influencer's phone rings first. A private announcement gives the caller's handle, prior call count and any note the influencer saved. Press <strong>1</strong> to accept or <strong>2</strong> to decline; no response within 10 seconds also declines. The caller is dialled only after acceptance, with no caller charge for a decline.</p>
<p>During a connected call, the influencer's <strong>*</strong> key ends it. The influencer's <strong>#</strong> key ends it, blocks that caller from that influencer and flags the incident for review. A report is not a confirmed strike. Both participants can always hang up normally.</p>
<h2>Still not confidential</h2>
<p>Calls in Women-only channels are recorded for safety and checked by AI after the call, like every call. Nobody listens live. The other person still hears everything you say, so decide what to share. Read the <a href="/safety">safety centre</a>.</p>
<h2>If something feels wrong</h2>
<p>End the call. Influencers can block, report or tag a caller through their dashboard or a post-call WhatsApp message. See <a href="/report">Report a user</a> for the reporting route. Keep the call ID and a short description; do not include identity documents. Reports are not an emergency response service.</p>
<p>Talking about distress or self-harm must not earn a strike. A platform report cannot replace outside help.</p>
<h2>Help outside the platform</h2>
<div class="hf-help-strip" aria-label="Independent helplines in India">
  <a href="tel:112"><strong>112</strong><span>Immediate danger</span></a>
  <a href="tel:181"><strong>181</strong><span>Women's support</span></a>
  <a href="tel:14416"><strong>14416</strong><span>Mental-health support</span></a>
  <a href="tel:1930"><strong>1930</strong><span>Online financial fraud</span></a>
</div>
<p>These are separate services, not {BRAND.name} support. See <a href="/emergency">Emergency support</a> or the official <a href="https://112.gov.in/">112</a>, <a href="https://missionshakti.wcd.gov.in/">Mission Shakti</a>, <a href="https://dghs.mohfw.gov.in/national-mental-health-programme.php">Tele-MANAS</a> and <a href="https://www.cybercrime.gov.in/">Cyber Crime Portal</a> pages.</p>
